						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#67">Bonestriker's Bounty</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							I'm introducing a new program for guildmates.  It's called &quot;Bonestriker's Bounty&quot;.  Its purpose is to help motivate people to recruit good, quality players to join our guild.<br />
<br />
Now, I don't want folks /shouting to the zone that we're looking for recruits -- that's not classy and it will make us look bad.  But what I'd like folks to do is to talk to folks they're playing with -- folks that have good personalities and know how to play their character.  In other words, someone they would trust and can count on in a pinch.<br />
<br />
Here are the terms.  For every person you recruit level 30-39, you get 1 credit.  If they also happen to be a cleric, druid, enchanter, or wizard, you get an extra credit (2 total).<br />
<br />
For every person level 40-49, you get 2 credits.  If they are a cleric, druid, enchanter, or wizard, you get an extra credit (3 total).<br />
<br />
For every person you recruit level 50-60, you get 3 credits.  And yes, you get an extra credit if they're a cleric/druid/enchanter/wizard.<br />
<br />
To get your credits, you need to have your new recruits go to http://www.guildsay.com, and they need to do the following.<br />
<br />
They need to create a login at guildsay.com, then they need to go to our guild page (click on &quot;Innoruuk&quot; under the &quot;choose a server&quot; then &quot;Crusaders of Ilk&quot;).  Once on our guild webpage they need to click on &quot;Create Character&quot;.  They need to enter their information, making sure to have &quot;Crusaders of Ilk&quot; as their guild, and to fill in the guild password &quot;Scaly&quot;.<br />
<br />
They then need to post a message to our message boards stating who they are, what class and level they are, and that they are a prospective new member who would love the opportunity to join.<br />
<br />
Once they have this done, you need to contact an officer and have them interview the person and if they seem fit, /guildinvite them.  You then would post a reply to their message stating that you recruited them.<br />
<br />
I'll keep a running total of Bonestriker's Bounty credits, and at the end of February, the person with the most credits gets 2000pp.  That's right, 2000pp.<br />
<br />
Good luck!<br />
Bonestriker.
						</td>
